{:edb/db-before-t 574 :edb/db-after-t 575 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533887 50 #inst "2026-10-05T08:22:14.044Z" 13194139533887 true] [17592186083156 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263416 13194139533887 true] [17592186083156 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263423 13194139533887 true] [17592186083156 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263444 13194139533887 true] [17592186083156 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263477 13194139533887 true] [17592186083156 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263502 13194139533887 true] [17592186083157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263430 13194139533887 true] [17592186083157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263437 13194139533887 true] [17592186083157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263458 13194139533887 true] [17592186083157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263465 13194139533887 true] [17592186083157 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263473 13194139533887 true] [17592186083245 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263451 13194139533887 true] [17592186083245 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263469 13194139533887 true] [17592186083245 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263481 13194139533887 true] [17592186083245 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263488 13194139533887 true] [17592186083245 1020 #edb/ref 17592186263495 13194139533887 true] [17592186263416 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263417 13194139533887 true] [17592186263416 1089 "q-117633" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263416 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533887 true] [17592186263416 1100 "Solve the equation $\\frac{2}{w-5}-\\frac{1}{3w}=\\frac{1}{{w}^{2}-5w}.$" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263416 1113 #uuid "2976a7b7-c5e4-571a-adf1-1879b7fb12b5" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263416 1145 "First, we factor the quadratic denominator, giving us the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{w-5}-\\frac{1}{3w}=\\frac{1}{w(w-5)}.\n$$\n\nWe now make the following observations:\n\n- The least common denominator of our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(w-5,\\,3w,\\,w(w-5))=3w(w-5).\n$$\n\n- The values $w=0$ and $w=5$ cannot be solutions to our equation. These values make at least one denominator in our original equation equal zero, and division by zero is undefined.\n\nNow, multiplying both sides of the equation by the least common denominator, we can simplify it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{w-5}-\\frac{1}{3w}=\\frac{1}{w(w-5)} \\\\ 3w(w-5)\\cdot (\\frac{2}{w-5}-\\frac{1}{3w}) & =3w(w-5)\\cdot \\frac{1}{w(w-5)} \\\\ \\frac{6w(w-5)}{w-5}-\\frac{3w(w-5)}{3w}=\\frac{3w(w-5)}{w(w-5)} \\\\ \\frac{6w\\cancel{(w-5)}}{\\cancel{w-5}}-\\frac{\\cancel{3w}(w-5)}{\\cancel{3w}}=\\frac{3\\cancel{w(w-5)}}{\\cancel{w(w-5)}} \\\\ 6w-(w-5) & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $w,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6w-(w-5) & =3 \\\\ 5w+5 & =3 \\\\ 5w & =-2 \\\\ w & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{2}{5}\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{2}{5}\\ne 5,$ we conclude that $w=-\\frac{2}{5}$ is a valid solution. \n\nTherefore, the solution to our original equation is $w=-\\frac{2}{5}.$" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263417 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263418 13194139533887 true] [17592186263417 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263419 13194139533887 true] [17592186263417 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263420 13194139533887 true] [17592186263417 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263421 13194139533887 true] [17592186263417 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263422 13194139533887 true] [17592186263417 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533887 true] [17592186263417 1041 "selection" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263417 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263420 13194139533887 true] [17592186263417 1110 #uuid "6cb2d30b-93d4-55b9-ad80-9bc2646a127f" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263418 1034 "No solutions" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533887 true] [17592186263418 1111 #uuid "d04118f4-a490-5479-9c81-a487b5c48d0d" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263419 1034 "w=-\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263419 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263419 1111 #uuid "3d82ef08-e7a5-5f13-a8b2-b4f5e9ebf104" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263420 1034 "w=-\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263420 1103 #edb/ref 17592186