following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2V-(2V+1) & =2 \\\\ 2V-2V-1 & =2 \\\\ -1 & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a false statement. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions." 13194139533887 true] [17592186263424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263425 13194139533887 true] [17592186263424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263426 13194139533887 true] [17592186263424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263427 13194139533887 true] [17592186263424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263428 13194139533887 true] [17592186263424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263429 13194139533887 true] [17592186263424 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533887 true] [17592186263424 1041 "selection" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263424 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263425 13194139533887 true] [17592186263424 1110 #uuid "ec110647-ce30-59a7-a377-7075e64038b0" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263425 1034 "No solutions" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263425 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533887 true] [17592186263425 1111 #uuid "aa329ace-559c-5888-a6a1-8bf9aa8b22f5" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263426 1034 "V=1" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263426 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263426 1111 #uuid "a5715624-6a1c-520f-ad76-fdd4edb736fc" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263427 1034 "V=2" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263427 1111 #uuid "2b88df5c-8220-5af5-a215-ae82ddc1184a" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263428 1034 "V=\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263428 1111 #uuid "8d059fbc-6802-5187-9fae-6eb45023b82a" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263429 1034 "V=\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263429 1111 #uuid "6af7b969-59ef-5c2d-b664-f2e8fb81ec88" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263430 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263431 13194139533887 true] [17592186263430 1089 "q-117682" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263430 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533887 true] [17592186263430 1100 "Solve the equation $\\frac{1}{2(V+4)}+\\frac{1}{V-4}=\\frac{8}{{V}^{2}-16}.$" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263430 1113 #uuid "add7ad15-a989-5880-8090-8af6c15fef69" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263430 1145 "First, we factor the quadratic denominator, giving us the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2(V+4)}+\\frac{1}{V-4}=\\frac{8}{(V+4)(V-4)}.\n$$\n\nWe now make the following observations:\n\n- The least common denominator of our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(2(V+4),\\,V-4,\\,(V+4)(V-4))=2(V+4)(V-4).\n$$\n\n- The values $V=-4$ and $V=4$ cannot be solutions to our equation. These values make at least one denominator in our original equation equal zero, and division by zero is undefined.\n\nNow, multiplying both sides of the equation by the least common denominator, we can simplify it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2(V+4)}+\\frac{1}{V-4} & =\\frac{8}{(V+4)(V-4)} \\\\ 2(V+4)(V-4)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2(V+4)}+\\frac{1}{V-4}) & =2(V+4)(V-4)\\cdot \\frac{8}{(V+4)(V-4)} \\\\ \\frac{2(V+4)(V-4)}{2(V+4)}+\\frac{2(V+4)(V-4)}{V-4} & =\\frac{16(V+4)(V-4)}{(V+4)(V-4)} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2(V+4)}(V-4)}{\\cancel{2(V+4)}}+\\frac{2(V+4)\\cancel{(V-4)}}{\\cancel{V-4}} & =\\frac{16\\cancel{(V+4)(V-4)}}{\\cancel{(V+4)(V-4)}} \\\\ (V-4)+2(V+4) & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $V,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(V-4)+2(V+4) & =16 \\\\ V-4+2V+8 & =16 \\\\ 3V & =12 \\\\ V & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $V=4$ is not a valid solution, our equation has no solutions." 13194139533887 true] [17592186263431 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263432 13194139533887 true] [17592186263431 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263433 13194139533887 true] [17592186263431 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263434 13194139533887 true] [17592186263431 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263435 13194139533887 true] [17592186263431 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263436 13194139533887 true] [17592186263431 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533887 true] [17592186263431 1041 "selection" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263431 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263432 13194139533887 true] [17592186263431 1110 #uuid "c9599e57-b1c0-5efe-9915-6354bc652808" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263432 1034 "No solutions" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263432 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533887 true] [17592186263432 1111 #uuid "016ef3cc-7d6e-56c4-8b26-7ce1164c6dd2" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263433 1034 "V=2" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263433 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263433 1111 #uuid "54a0baeb-d794-51da-83b9-446a4b0369b5" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263434 1034 "V=3" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263434 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263434 1111 #uuid "408557e6-173c-50ce-87df-15446b7c4752" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263435 1034 "V=\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263435 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263435 1111 #uuid "bb2cdf5f-d77a-5ff4-8a1e-87d171e12c5c" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263436 1034 "V=\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263436 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263436 1111 #uuid "a198d35e-c8a2-541d-ab6f-5ee29a4dbd76" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263437 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263438 13194139533887 true] [17592186263437 1089 "q-117688" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263437 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533887 true] [17592186263437 1100 "Solve the equation $\\frac{1}{2(s+4)}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+3s-4}.$" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263437 1113 #uuid "54fb83dc-f3f4-5e13-91b2-57b93c857b79" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263437 1145 "First, we factor the quadratic denominator, giving us the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2(s+4)}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{(s+4)(s-1)}.\n$$\n\nWe now make the following observations:\n\n- The least common denominator of our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(2(s+4),\\,s-1,\\,(s+4)(s-1)))=2(s+4)(s-1).\n$$\n\n- The values $s=-4$ and $s=1$ cannot be solutions to our equation. These values make at least one denominator in our original equation equal zero, and division by zero is undefined.\n\nNow, multiplying both sides of the equation by the least common denominator, we can simplify it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2(s+4)} & =\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{(s+4)(s-1)} \\\\ 2(s+4)(s-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2(s+4)} & =2(s+4)(s-1)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{(s+4)(s-1)}) \\\\ \\frac{2(s+4)(s-1)}{2(s+4)} & =\\frac{2(s+4)(s-1)}{s-1}-\\frac{6(s+4)(s-1)}{(s+4)(s-1)} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2(s+4)}(s-1)}{\\cancel{2(s+4)}} & =\\frac{2(s+4)\\cancel{(s-1)}}{\\cancel{s-1}}-\\frac{6\\cancel{(s+4)(s-1)}}{\\cancel{(s+4)(s-1)}} \\\\ (s-1) & =2(s+4)-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $s,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1) & =2(s+4)-6 \\\\ s-1 & =2s+2 \\\\ s & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-3\\ne -4$ and $-3\\ne 1,$ we conclude that $s=-3$ is a valid solution. \n\nTherefore, the solution to our original equation is $s=-3.$" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263438 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263439 13194139533887 true] [17592186263438 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263440 13194139533887 true] [17592186263438 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263441 13194139533887 true] [17592186263438 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263442 13194139533887 true] [17592186263438 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263443 13194139533887 true] [17592186263438 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533887 true] [17592186263438 1041 "selection" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263438 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263442 13194139533887 true] [17592186263438 1110 #uuid "563eab5f-3e1b-56ee-9833-f8fbfb52a103" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263439 1034 "s=\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263439 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263439 1111 #uuid "3194bcaa-9628-5ad2-b02d-746f11462748" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263440 1034 "s=\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263440 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263440 1111 #uu