)}{\\cancel{x+1}} \\\\ x+1 & =5-2(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving this equation for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =5-2(x-1) \\\\ x+1 & =5-2x+2 \\\\ 3x & =6 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $2\\ne -1$ and $2\\ne 1,$ we conclude that $x=2$ is a valid solution. \n\nTherefore, the solution to our original equation is $x=2.$" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263467 13194139533887 true] [17592186263466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263468 13194139533887 true] [17592186263466 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533887 true] [17592186263466 1041 "field-1" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263466 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263468 13194139533887 true] [17592186263466 1110 #uuid "33bad834-b414-5d19-9519-104c3ed97282" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263467 1034 "3" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263467 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263467 1111 #uuid "7840a230-6a23-5bf9-92a2-d629c386a1ba" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263468 1034 "2" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263468 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533887 true] [17592186263468 1111 #uuid "5276abfb-9a18-586e-8ff0-6f2784e5927e" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263469 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263470 13194139533887 true] [17592186263469 1089 "q-276459" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263469 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533887 true] [17592186263469 1100 "Solve the equation $\\frac{3}{n+4}-\\frac{5}{n(n+4)}=\\frac{2}{n}.$\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263469 1113 #uuid "9b8e89a0-6a6d-5b9e-b505-b40b9b084524" 13194139533887 true] [17592186263469 1145 "We make the following observations:\n\n- The least common denominator of our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(n+4,\\,n(n+4),\\,n)=n(n+4).\n$$\n\n- The values $n=-4$ and $n=0$ cannot be solutions to our equation. These values make at least one denominator in our original equation equal zero, and division by zero is undefined.\n\nNow, multiplying both sides of the equation by 